{
 "id": "media/big-image-hot-request-op-over-media/5m",
 "description": "Request 0 caches one 500-token message. Request 1 (30 seconds later, hot) adds a 2,000,000-byte image and an 8,000-byte message. A rewrite cuts the image to 1,000,000 bytes. The bill is 2,350 tokens, below the library price of the forwarded image (1,000,000 / 250 = 4,000). Forwarded text = 2,000 + 8,000 = 10,000 bytes; the least is 0.05 x 10,000 = 500 tokens; the media gets 2,350 - 500 = 1,850 tokens. The client media is 2,000,000 bytes = 3,700 tokens, so the bill difference is 500 + 3,700 - 2,350 = 1,850 tokens: all of it is the image the rewrite removed. The rewrite covers media, so it is unpriced (media_tokens), and the check conservation takes its 1,850 tokens out of the bill difference. Only media_tokens fails. Before the fix conservation failed too.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#accountant-42",
